                <h2>Alternative Airports in Hawaii</h2>
                <p>While Honolulu dominates, strategic travelers may consider island-specific alternatives.</p>
                <h3>Kahului Airport (OGG), Maui</h3>
                <p>Best for dedicated Maui vacations.</p>
                <p><b>Strategic value:</b><p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Direct seasonal service from some mainland cities</li>
                        <li>Bypasses Honolulu entirely for Maui-focused trips</li>
                        <li>Proximity to Haleakalā, Road to Hana, and Molokini Crater</li>
                    </ul>
                    <h3>Kona International Airport (KOA), Big Island</h3>
                <p>Optimal for volcanic exploration.</p>
                <p><b>Considerations:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Direct seasonal service from select mainland gateways</li>
                    <li>Close to Hawaii Volcanoes National Park</li>
                    <li>Sunny Kona coast versus rainy Hilo side</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Lihue Airport (LIH), Kauai</h3>
                <p>Ideal for Garden Isle immersion.</p>
                <p><b>Realities:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Limited direct mainland service</li>
                    <li>Most connections through Honolulu</li>
                    <li>Smaller facility; quicker processing</li>
                </ul>
                <h3>Hilo International Airport (ITO), Big Island</h3>
                <p>Best for eastern Big Island and volcanic exploration.</p>
                <p><b>Profile:</b></p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Limited service; primarily inter-island and some mainland</li>
                    <li>Close to Hawaii Volcanoes National Park</li>
                    <li>Rainy side of the island; lush vegetation</li>
                </ul>
